OL,3,AYou may get the right to find out what
OL,4,Ayour colleagues earn - here's why
OL,5,
OL,6,FEmployees should legally be able to
OL,7,Ffind out what their colleagues are
OL,8,Fearning, the UK's equality watchdog has
OL,9,Fsaid.
OL,11,FBosses should be required to respond to
OL,12,Fquestionaires about colleagues' pay to
OL,13,Fcut pay discrimination, the Equality
OL,14,Fand Human Rights Commission (EHRC) has
OL,15,Fproposed.
OL,17,FIn addition, employers should be
OL,18,Fprevented from asking about current
OL,19,Fsalary when offering a job to stop a
OL,20,Fhistory of discrimination from carrying
OL,21,Fon, it said.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
